FlashNX is an integration layer for Nintendo Switch built on top of Ruffle
(https://github.com/ruffle-rs/ruffle, Apache-2.0 / MIT) and other third-party
projects (devkitPro/libnx, switch-mesa, libcurl, Mbed-TLS, zlib, jpeg-decoder,
and various Rust crates). Those components remain under their own respective
licenses; see the "Crédits & licences" section of README.md for details.

The FlashNX integration code itself is released under the MIT License (see LICENSE).
